      "text": "Proposition 5.1 (conditional on GRH). There are inﬁnitely many primes p, inert in K, for which the order of ǫ in (OK/pOK)× is precisely δ(p + 1). (In fact, Roskam shows that the order is δ(p+1) not only for inﬁnitely many inert primes, but for a positive proportion of all inert primes. The weaker version here is suﬃcient for our purposes.) Theorem 1.4 is an immediate consequence of Proposition 5.1 in conjunction with the next assertion.",
